WEBVTT

00:10.301 --> 00:12.053
LOOKING FOR THE SEX VIDEO OF THIS GIRL

00:13.972 --> 00:16.182
DO YOU KNOW THIS GIRL?
IT'S HARD TO GET HER VIDEO

00:16.266 --> 00:18.893
HEARD SHE KILLED HERSELF
YOU REALLY WANNA JACK OFF TO THIS?

00:18.977 --> 00:21.312
BUT I SAW A PIC OF HER
WORKING AS A FLORIST

00:26.443 --> 00:29.696
"Why can't you take my word for it
and just believe me? She's dead."

00:29.779 --> 00:32.741
SHE'S DEAD. THE FLORIST THING IS A LIE.

01:27.295 --> 01:31.216
A KILLER PARADOX

01:48.608 --> 01:52.028
RESIDENT IDENTIFICATION CERTIFICATE
LEE GYEONG-SU

02:08.503 --> 02:10.672
Superman flies through the sky.

02:11.506 --> 02:13.591
Spider-Man shoots out webs.

02:15.051 --> 02:18.555
And Lee Tang carries out retribution.

02:21.558 --> 02:25.186
Those who are detected on Lee Tang's radar
are all criminals

02:25.270 --> 02:26.688
who dodged laws made by men.

02:28.356 --> 02:30.150
-And deserved to die.
-Bitch.

02:32.360 --> 02:35.071
-No, they're all human garbage.
-What do you want?

02:35.655 --> 02:36.656
Professor, please.

02:36.739 --> 02:40.285
If you got pregnant, then you should've
gotten an abortion. So go!

02:41.369 --> 02:42.537
It's your baby, though.

02:42.620 --> 02:44.873
Stupid whore! How dare you?

02:45.373 --> 02:46.875
MURDERED PROFESSOR WAS A KILLER

02:46.958 --> 02:50.545
Retribution isn't bound
by laws or ethics. It's pure and absolute.

02:51.421 --> 02:54.007
A crime always leaves behind evidence,

02:56.259 --> 02:58.928
but retribution is beyond
something humans can prove.

02:59.762 --> 03:03.141
Emotions will get the better of
he who murders for vengeance,

03:03.224 --> 03:06.352
and punishment
for those who murder in malice.

03:09.272 --> 03:14.068
But Lee Tang's murders are not
swayed by emotions or punishment.

03:14.777 --> 03:16.946
They are the essence of pure good

03:17.989 --> 03:19.574
and absolute justice.

03:22.911 --> 03:25.622
No one can take these criminals to trial,

03:27.081 --> 03:28.833
but someone must act,

03:30.251 --> 03:33.546
even though not a person
in the world will ever know about it.

03:41.471 --> 03:44.807
Gyeong-su, what'd you do
before this? Were you a student?

03:44.891 --> 03:45.808
No.

03:46.434 --> 03:48.436
You wanna open up your own store, or what?

03:48.937 --> 03:49.854
No.

03:49.938 --> 03:53.691
Oh… So, then, why'd you come
all this way out to Busan?

03:54.651 --> 03:58.279
You know, these Gen Z kids hate it
when you bombard them with questions.

03:58.363 --> 04:01.074
-That's not true. They enjoy it.
-You can just ignore her.

04:01.157 --> 04:03.993
Gyeong-a, we're a family here.
Why are you acting this way?

04:04.077 --> 04:06.913
Seon-gyeong is home until tomorrow
because she's sick.

04:06.996 --> 04:08.748
I'm not asking for a huge favor.

04:09.249 --> 04:12.919
Shouldn't you be hiring
a new cashier then, sir?

04:13.002 --> 04:16.256
-Oh my God. There she goes again.
-Are you serious? Really?

04:16.339 --> 04:19.217
-We need all the help we can get!
-Kids these days are all so rude.

04:19.717 --> 04:23.346
-Doesn't care about anyone but herself.
-Come on, get serious.

04:23.429 --> 04:24.597
-Honestly!
-Yes, but…

04:24.681 --> 04:28.309
She's the worst. Since she started,
I don't think she's ever said hello.

04:28.393 --> 04:30.353
And she never goes out with us.

04:30.436 --> 04:33.273
Hey, the girl's probably
just busy with her boyfriend.

04:33.356 --> 04:35.191
Are you making a fuss 'cause she's pretty?

04:35.275 --> 04:39.112
Hah! What do you mean, pretty?
She's probably had her whole face done.

04:39.195 --> 04:42.490
And what's the point of plastic surgery
when you're stuck in a warehouse?

04:42.573 --> 04:44.909
Okay, I'll get it done after this.

04:44.993 --> 04:46.953
It's always "after this." I'll do it.

04:47.036 --> 04:49.163
No one's at the register. Get to it.

04:50.748 --> 04:53.418
Please, okay? Thank you.

04:54.335 --> 04:55.753
Oh, Seung-hun.

04:56.462 --> 04:58.923
"The homeroom rep
and Choi In-seon fought today."

04:59.007 --> 05:00.925
"The homeroom rep totally made fun of her

05:01.009 --> 05:03.261
and said the mole on her nose
looks like a weird booger."

05:03.344 --> 05:06.180
The homeroom rep had
a crush on her too.

05:06.681 --> 05:07.849
A love triangle?

05:08.433 --> 05:10.768
Pfft. That's adorable.

05:10.852 --> 05:11.894
WE'RE GETTING MARRIED

05:11.978 --> 05:13.813
THANK YOU FOR COMING TO CELEBRATE

05:16.649 --> 05:18.359
-Oppa.
-Mm-hmm?

05:18.443 --> 05:20.069
-When are you gonna be done?
-Oh, whoa!

05:20.153 --> 05:21.863
-Do you still have a lot to do?
-Why?

05:21.946 --> 05:23.740
-How much do you have left?
-Mm?

05:23.823 --> 05:25.033
When will you be done?

05:25.116 --> 05:27.702
I'm all done. I'm all done.

05:27.785 --> 05:29.954
-Finished.
-Aren't I heavy?

05:30.038 --> 05:33.666
Not at all. Why can't you
just leave me alone, hmm?

05:33.750 --> 05:36.294
-Kiss me. Kiss me.
-What took you so long, huh?

06:05.031 --> 06:06.157
Excuse me!

06:07.742 --> 06:11.913
This is exactly like last time.
This supermarket has terrible service.

06:11.996 --> 06:15.041
What, do you think your work's
done after you sell the goods? Huh?

06:15.541 --> 06:17.919
Customers have to keep
a stupid file of receipts now?

06:18.002 --> 06:21.297
You say you bought this three days ago?

06:21.381 --> 06:23.674
Forget it, come on!
I'm busy. Just hurry already.

06:24.175 --> 06:26.594
Hey, if you don't know, just ask. Come on!

06:26.677 --> 06:30.431
I'm searching for the purchase
you made to print the receipt for you,

06:30.515 --> 06:31.766
but I don't see it here.

06:31.849 --> 06:34.018
What the hell are you mumbling about?

06:34.102 --> 06:37.313
Where else do you think I would've bought
this crap, if it wasn't from here?

06:38.022 --> 06:41.609
What are you looking at?
Don't give me that look, you little hussy!

06:41.692 --> 06:43.403
Are you trying to pick a fight with me?

06:43.486 --> 06:44.821
-Come on, then!
-Ma'am.

06:44.904 --> 06:47.281
I'm sorry. I think she just
made a mistake.

06:47.365 --> 06:49.784
-Give her a refund
-What's with this supermarket?

06:49.867 --> 06:51.452
All I did was ask for a refund!

06:55.581 --> 06:58.918
Ma'am, I'll make sure
this doesn't happen again. I'm so sorry.

06:59.001 --> 07:02.004
Thank you for understanding.
Here, this is on the house.

07:02.088 --> 07:03.172
I'm sorry again.

07:04.799 --> 07:05.883
Drive safely.

07:15.601 --> 07:16.519
What?

07:20.565 --> 07:23.651
Hey. Hey, did you do
this to my windshield?

07:27.363 --> 07:30.450
Have you completely
lost your damn mind? Huh?

07:30.992 --> 07:31.993
Are you crazy?

07:32.952 --> 07:35.288
I asked you a question! Jeez.

07:35.371 --> 07:36.956
What if I didn't do it?

07:37.457 --> 07:38.583
Will you say sorry?

07:39.417 --> 07:40.293
What?

07:41.669 --> 07:44.589
You shouldn't accuse
if you don't have any proof.

07:46.007 --> 07:48.885
I guess you're too ignorant
and dumb to know better,

07:48.968 --> 07:50.845
but you messed with the wrong lady.

07:51.679 --> 07:55.099
I have a dashcam.
I'm not letting this slide.

07:55.975 --> 07:58.269
-Are you nuts? Unbelievable!
-Fine, report it.

07:58.352 --> 08:01.898
I'm sure the dashcam caught you stealing
from that pile and demanding a refund.

08:05.401 --> 08:06.277
What?

08:08.070 --> 08:08.988
Make your call.

08:10.281 --> 08:11.365
I'm…

08:12.283 --> 08:14.410
-Should I call?
-Hey. What are you doing?

08:17.413 --> 08:19.332
-I don't have time for this!
-Well?

08:20.541 --> 08:21.375
It's…

08:22.418 --> 08:23.836
it's not that.

08:23.920 --> 08:26.255
Then what? Huh?

08:26.339 --> 08:29.175
You won't even answer the customers
when they ask a question.

08:29.258 --> 08:31.093
Why do you act this way? Huh?

08:31.177 --> 08:32.929
I told you about this last time.

08:33.012 --> 08:33.930
I'm sorry.

08:57.537 --> 08:59.080
-Fish section, right?
-Yeah.

09:04.377 --> 09:05.461
Why'd you come here?

09:15.221 --> 09:16.097
Listen.

09:17.014 --> 09:19.100
I think you're a lot like me, actually.

09:21.018 --> 09:21.894
I am?

09:26.315 --> 09:28.818
You know, I've been noticing how…

09:29.986 --> 09:32.863
how you change the subject
when they ask about your past,

09:32.947 --> 09:35.116
and how you keep your
distance from others.

09:35.783 --> 09:37.577
And you're probably in your 20s,

09:37.660 --> 09:41.122
but got a job at a small supermarket
that's really far away.

09:42.123 --> 09:42.999
Aah.

09:44.667 --> 09:48.045
And, uh, you're rude to asshole customers.

09:48.129 --> 09:49.171
I feel like…

09:50.172 --> 09:51.674
like we have that in common.

09:55.803 --> 09:57.430
I'm like that, huh?

09:59.640 --> 10:01.058
Well, if not, forget it.

10:04.562 --> 10:06.439
Aren't you tired of people here

10:07.607 --> 10:10.234
being gossipy
and in your business all the time?

10:13.779 --> 10:16.657
Although, they're not all that bad,
to be honest.

10:17.158 --> 10:20.578
Mm… They normally nag
you and act annoying.

10:21.245 --> 10:24.749
Except they usually quit
after the first month that you're here.

10:26.334 --> 10:28.252
I didn't get to have that, though,

10:29.754 --> 10:30.880
so it's hard.

10:35.468 --> 10:36.344
What's that?

10:38.471 --> 10:41.307
Well, being, I guess, normal.

10:41.390 --> 10:43.559
I mean, living a normal life.

10:46.729 --> 10:48.856
You know, I'm just kinda…

10:50.941 --> 10:53.903
tired of having big dreams anymore.

10:54.487 --> 10:58.908
Just… living an ordinary life
seems to be the key.

11:27.687 --> 11:30.523
Please take a step back
from the yellow line.

11:32.024 --> 11:33.234
I repeat.

11:33.984 --> 11:38.531
The KTX train scheduled
to arrive in Busan at 9:50 a.m…

11:38.614 --> 11:40.991
LOOKING FOR THE SEX VIDEO OF THIS GIRL

11:41.075 --> 11:42.785
DO YOU KNOW THIS GIRL?

11:42.868 --> 11:43.911
IS THIS HER?

11:43.994 --> 11:45.579
…from the yellow line.

11:49.959 --> 11:52.503
UPDATE ON THE GIRL
FROM THE UNIVERSITY OF EDUCATION

11:52.586 --> 11:55.089
THE REPUBLIC OF PLASTIC SURGERY
WHERE DID YOU GET THIS?

12:01.804 --> 12:03.764
Mom! Mom.

12:04.265 --> 12:05.933
Hey, come help me with these.

12:07.518 --> 12:11.063
Why'd you bring all this? You should've
just had it all shipped over.

12:11.147 --> 12:13.399
The move must have you pretty busy.

12:13.482 --> 12:16.110
Why ship it when I can just bring it?

12:16.193 --> 12:18.821
How's that going?
Are you doing door-to-door service?

12:18.904 --> 12:21.198
No. Don't you know
how far we're moving?

12:21.282 --> 12:23.576
Are you nuts? How are you gonna do it all?

12:24.243 --> 12:26.871
I'm just organizing
and throwing stuff out.

12:26.954 --> 12:28.789
Think it's easy starting a new life?

12:28.873 --> 12:31.375
Gosh.
So, did Dad head there already?

12:31.459 --> 12:32.585
What about In-jun?

12:32.668 --> 12:34.879
They both went
to finish the greenhouse.

12:34.962 --> 12:36.255
Check if that's yours.

12:36.338 --> 12:38.507
Hey, what'd you bring these for?

12:41.886 --> 12:43.137
What's this doing here?

12:43.220 --> 12:45.973
I had it terminated
at the community service center.

12:46.515 --> 12:49.185
Remember, you got another one
because you had lost it?

12:49.685 --> 12:51.312
I found that one in the closet.

12:54.815 --> 12:56.400
IDENTIFICATION
CHOI IN-SEON, CHOI GYEONG-A

12:56.484 --> 12:57.359
Gyeong-a.

12:59.403 --> 13:00.988
You'll visit us often, right?

13:02.364 --> 13:03.365
Hmm?

13:03.866 --> 13:06.368
You don't need a reason
to come home, you know.

13:07.787 --> 13:10.164
Why are you suddenly bringing that up now?

13:11.207 --> 13:15.085
We have a room for you in the new house.
Now you can visit whenever you want.

13:15.711 --> 13:17.797
Think of it more like a fun sabbatical.

13:26.138 --> 13:27.056
Hey.

13:27.556 --> 13:31.477
Look at you. You're
glowin' after a little time off. Jesus.

13:32.728 --> 13:35.689
You haven't even opened it.
Didn't you get that last summer?

13:38.442 --> 13:40.694
You got a nice place,
but you need a woman in here.

13:40.778 --> 13:42.530
Smells like a bachelor pad.

13:42.613 --> 13:44.323
Whoa! What--

13:45.574 --> 13:48.244
Hey, isn't this the…
the dog from that girl's case?

13:49.370 --> 13:52.039
Dang, well, we can't just
send him away somewhere.

13:52.706 --> 13:54.500
We can't put him down, either.

13:55.459 --> 13:57.628
Should a detective raise a dog, though?

13:58.212 --> 14:00.631
I brought him here
hoping he might bring me luck

14:00.714 --> 14:03.092
with all of the ongoing investigations.

14:03.592 --> 14:06.011
I'm just keeping him
until he's proven innocent.

14:06.720 --> 14:09.765
Didn't you say you have some time
before you leave? Why are you here?

14:11.642 --> 14:13.936
Well, it's what's-his-face.

14:14.019 --> 14:16.146
Right, Roh Bin.

14:16.647 --> 14:18.274
Don't go near him, all right?

14:18.357 --> 14:21.318
It's thanks to the captain
you only got a restraining order.

14:21.402 --> 14:24.822
If he decides to press charges
against you, your ass is done for, buddy.

14:24.905 --> 14:28.701
How am I supposed to investigate when
I can't even get his security cam footage?

14:28.784 --> 14:31.203
You came here to tell me that?

14:32.705 --> 14:34.456
No. Listen.

14:35.207 --> 14:36.083
You…

14:36.917 --> 14:39.295
Look, why aren't
you answering anybody's calls?

14:40.212 --> 14:42.089
Did Yong-jae say I wasn't pickin' up?

14:42.172 --> 14:44.925
He keeps on callin' me
'cause you never answer.

14:45.009 --> 14:45.885
So?

14:46.886 --> 14:49.471
-So I told him to come.
-Come where? Here?

14:51.015 --> 14:52.266
-Now?
-Yeah.

14:52.349 --> 14:53.809
You owe me, sir.

14:55.561 --> 14:57.813
I'm really sorry
about the Kang Sang-muk incident.

14:57.897 --> 15:00.441
And I only received a warning
because you kept me in the dark

15:00.524 --> 15:02.776
about the situation
at Roh Bin's house, right?

15:03.360 --> 15:04.945
But if you had trusted me, sir,

15:05.029 --> 15:07.197
and shared information
for the investigation,

15:07.281 --> 15:10.910
we might've caught both Lee Tang
and that nerd without getting suspended.

15:10.993 --> 15:13.370
I'm so frustrated that I can't even sleep.

15:14.663 --> 15:17.124
I'm gonna catch that asshole, sir.

15:21.211 --> 15:24.673
Look how much he has to say.
Imagine how upset he was you ignored him.

15:26.216 --> 15:27.301
There you go. Good.

15:27.384 --> 15:31.513
Imagine that there's a line between here,
and cut across in one go.

15:31.597 --> 15:33.140
That's it! Yeah, great.

15:33.223 --> 15:34.558
-Look at that.
-Oh, God.

15:34.642 --> 15:38.062
He just needs to clean. What the heck
are you teaching him all that for?

15:38.145 --> 15:39.521
You should come check him out.

15:40.022 --> 15:42.066
He got the bones out perfectly.

15:42.149 --> 15:44.735
This right here is not an easy task.

15:44.818 --> 15:47.154
-Yeah, he's okay.
-This is how you learn.

15:47.237 --> 15:49.031
It's awkward and kinda tricky at first,

15:49.114 --> 15:52.576
but then, after a little practice,
you get used to it, hmm?

15:53.410 --> 15:54.912
You keep goin' like that,

15:54.995 --> 15:57.456
and you'll be able
to open up a shop in no time.

15:57.539 --> 15:58.666
So keep at it, kid.

16:15.891 --> 16:17.935
Heard about
Professor No's murder in Busan?

16:19.478 --> 16:20.354
Yeah.

16:20.437 --> 16:23.774
When he disappeared that day,
he moved to Busan. Lee Tang.

16:25.734 --> 16:26.568
Hmm.

16:26.652 --> 16:29.154
Oh, we found this by chance
while working on another case.

16:29.238 --> 16:31.448
-Huh! Chance, my ass.
-Well, did you know?

16:32.116 --> 16:33.492
Hey, look at this.

16:34.618 --> 16:37.496
This right here is
the murder of a drug dealer in Busan,

16:37.579 --> 16:40.374
and this, over here,
is the loan shark murder case.

16:40.457 --> 16:43.460
Hey, that…
that guy was murdered by a junkie,

16:43.544 --> 16:45.921
and the other guy died in a gang fight.

16:46.005 --> 16:48.173
And they couldn't find the culprit
for either case.

16:48.257 --> 16:51.343
So, what are you gonna do, then?
Do you even have a warrant?

16:52.177 --> 16:53.679
I know.

16:53.762 --> 16:56.348
We should go to Busan first.

16:57.224 --> 17:01.145
The cases in Daejeon are all closed now.
And we don't have an APB on him.

17:02.604 --> 17:04.732
Are you any good with emotional appeals?

17:07.067 --> 17:09.403
If I were the one reading this letter,

17:10.029 --> 17:12.656
I'd feel worried and perplexed also, yeah.

17:14.116 --> 17:15.784
-They told us he's an adult.
-Yeah.

17:15.868 --> 17:18.620
That he said
he was planning to take a working holiday,

17:18.704 --> 17:20.372
and that he even left a letter.

17:21.123 --> 17:24.168
So they suggested that we report him
as a runaway, not as missing.

17:24.251 --> 17:25.711
-Mm-hmm.
-So we just left.

17:25.794 --> 17:26.837
Yes, um…

17:27.421 --> 17:31.133
I want you to know
that you can legally report him missing.

17:32.009 --> 17:34.845
What? I don't get it. What's going on?

17:35.345 --> 17:38.849
How come the cops are saying two different
things about the same exact case?

17:38.932 --> 17:41.060
-Do they have different laws?
-This must be confusing--

17:41.143 --> 17:44.021
-Honey, no, please. I--
-They want to help us, all right? Please.

17:44.104 --> 17:47.107
-So, what is it that you'd like from us?
-Uh-huh.

17:47.191 --> 17:50.611
Uh, well, you can start
by reporting him missing again to me.

17:51.862 --> 17:54.573
If there's even a small chance
that someone is connected to a crime,

17:54.656 --> 17:56.325
then you can report them missing.

17:56.408 --> 17:57.284
-That's even--
-Wait.

17:57.367 --> 18:01.413
-Are you telling us he's a victim?
-No, that's not exactly what I'm saying.

18:01.497 --> 18:04.541
-What are you saying?
-Are you saying he committed a crime?

18:04.625 --> 18:05.501
-Uh…
-Hmm?

18:05.584 --> 18:07.920
As you can see right here, very well,

18:08.003 --> 18:10.672
he even asked
if we could use his security deposit

18:10.756 --> 18:12.466
to pay the store owner.

18:12.549 --> 18:14.051
-That's who he is.
-Yes. I see.

18:14.134 --> 18:16.804
-How can a kid like that commit a crime?
-Yes, I'm saying your son--

18:16.887 --> 18:19.389
What about… What do you call it?
Uh, voice phishing?

18:19.473 --> 18:22.726
-Or a cult or something? Is that what he--
-Ah, no, sir, it's not that.

18:22.810 --> 18:24.311
-You don't--
-Stop talking nonsense!

18:24.394 --> 18:27.481
So, what I think is
you need to find your son.

18:27.564 --> 18:28.649
-Of course.
-Yeah.

18:28.732 --> 18:30.943
-That is the most crucial thing right now.
-Exactly.

18:31.026 --> 18:32.152
-Right.
-This is frustrating.

18:32.236 --> 18:35.572
All right, guys. Let's just
hear them out first. You…

18:36.615 --> 18:38.575
You're not here to help us, are you?

18:40.160 --> 18:42.454
-I, uh… We'll help you find--
-No.

18:43.122 --> 18:43.997
No.

18:46.834 --> 18:49.545
We've actually come here
to ask you for your help.

18:52.714 --> 18:54.842
Then please, just be honest with us here.

18:55.551 --> 18:57.302
And then we'll make a decision.

18:59.555 --> 19:03.392
Like your mom said,
he doesn't have the guts to do that. Huh?

19:03.475 --> 19:06.353
-Mm…
-I know exactly how these cops operate.

19:06.436 --> 19:09.189
They go poking around
just based on a hunch.

19:10.023 --> 19:11.358
Don't worry too much.

19:11.859 --> 19:13.694
I thought they were strange too.

19:14.778 --> 19:16.113
How could they think…

19:16.780 --> 19:18.949
This whole thing's just ridiculous.

19:19.533 --> 19:20.993
Mom has a good point.

19:21.076 --> 19:22.828
Uh, Ma, I'm gonna go, okay?

19:22.911 --> 19:25.205
-Can you take a look at this for me?
-Hmm?

19:25.706 --> 19:28.458
Do you get something like this
even if you're abroad?

19:28.542 --> 19:30.544
RESERVE FORCES TRAINING NOTIFICATION
TO MR. LEE TANG

19:30.627 --> 19:31.503
BUSAN STATION

19:31.587 --> 19:33.630
Mm, this is delicious.

19:33.714 --> 19:35.382
Your dad hates this type of food.

19:35.465 --> 19:38.177
I only eat at places like this with you.

19:38.260 --> 19:40.721
Well, enjoy. You still
have time before your train.

19:40.804 --> 19:42.639
-Hmm?
-Your brother's just like your dad.

19:42.723 --> 19:45.309
He never takes me to nice places.

19:45.392 --> 19:48.020
-My daughter's the best.
-I wonder what it'll be tomorrow.

19:48.103 --> 19:49.730
You're addicted at this point.

19:50.814 --> 19:52.649
Seriously.

19:52.733 --> 19:53.942
No, I'm not.

19:54.026 --> 19:57.905
Ugh. It's seven already.
I really don't wanna go back to Seoul.

19:57.988 --> 19:59.198
-Drink water.
-I--

19:59.281 --> 20:01.617
Eat while it's hot.

20:06.038 --> 20:07.831
I'm sorry about this.

20:09.708 --> 20:12.169
I tried,
but I just can't let this one slide.

20:18.091 --> 20:18.967
Hey.

20:19.676 --> 20:22.137
-Wait, aren't you--
-What are you staring at? Hmm?

20:23.055 --> 20:26.767
What's mesmerizing enough to make you
keep staring at someone while they eat?

20:26.850 --> 20:28.977
-What is it?
-No, no, I'm not--

20:29.061 --> 20:32.898
Seeing a girl from a sex video
in real life got you turned on? That it?

20:32.981 --> 20:35.692
-Wait, uh, that's not why I stared.
-Oh, no?

20:36.318 --> 20:39.780
Why, huh? You little shits
can't even talk about it outright.

20:39.863 --> 20:42.991
-I thought you were someone I knew.
-Yes, I'm her.

20:43.617 --> 20:46.995
-I'm the girl in the video.
-No, that's not… It's just, uh…

20:48.288 --> 20:50.540
You went to Kwonseong Elementary.

20:53.293 --> 20:54.544
Aren't you Choi In-seon?

20:55.921 --> 20:57.631
It's me, Ha Sang-min.

21:00.259 --> 21:02.094
Well, um…

21:03.053 --> 21:05.722
Your mom,
she owned the snack shop near school.

21:05.806 --> 21:08.183
Yeah. And she looked familiar, so…

21:11.478 --> 21:15.107
Mm.
So, when did you come down to Busan?

21:16.692 --> 21:20.153
It was about, um,
this time last year, I think, so…

21:20.237 --> 21:22.114
-I see.
-I'm going back to Seoul next year.

21:22.197 --> 21:26.660
Oh, you are?
Still, you were here for a while. Mm.

21:30.330 --> 21:33.875
Did something go down?
I hadn't heard anything, but…

21:35.419 --> 21:37.713
Yeah, you heard it tonight, already.

21:39.673 --> 21:41.216
So, that's that. Mm.

21:43.176 --> 21:44.177
Hmm.

21:48.181 --> 21:50.600
You, um, removed your mole, didn't you?

21:50.684 --> 21:52.269
Ah, that's right.

21:52.352 --> 21:54.813
That was the first thing
I took care of.

22:02.070 --> 22:03.280
Oh, booger face!

22:04.656 --> 22:06.116
Wait, you don't remember?

22:06.199 --> 22:08.076
What did you say?

22:08.160 --> 22:11.163
-Booger face! You know?
-What?

22:11.663 --> 22:14.541
I recently read my childhood journal,
a little while ago,

22:14.624 --> 22:17.169
and, um… I had written about you.

22:17.252 --> 22:19.504
And it reminded me
of that little booger joke.

22:19.588 --> 22:21.048
What?

22:21.548 --> 22:25.510
Ah, come on.
How come you still have that old journal?

22:26.428 --> 22:28.597
It's nice to walk down memory lane.

22:32.309 --> 22:34.144
Right by the beach. Nice.

22:34.227 --> 22:37.481
Thanks for the ride.
I can get home by myself from here.

22:37.564 --> 22:39.816
-Mm.
-Sorry about earlier today.

22:39.900 --> 22:40.984
No, it's cool.

22:41.068 --> 22:43.653
Hey, is it okay if we stay in touch?

22:44.613 --> 22:46.531
Oh… actually…

22:47.032 --> 22:50.869
Let's not see each other anymore.
I think I'd be more comfortable with that.

22:52.329 --> 22:53.955
I gotta go. See ya.

22:54.998 --> 22:55.874
Bye.

23:11.598 --> 23:13.350
How can I help you, ma'am?

23:15.685 --> 23:16.561
Hello.

23:17.229 --> 23:19.022
Hi, ma'am. Thanks for coming.

23:19.940 --> 23:23.026
-We brought you this.
-Oh, right, right. Thank you.

23:29.282 --> 23:31.368
REQUESTING COOPERATION
IN MISSING PERSON SEARCH

24:00.397 --> 24:02.858
Lee Tang. Lee Tang?
His name is Lee Tang?

24:02.941 --> 24:05.735
-Yeah.
-That's a pretty unique name, huh?

24:06.862 --> 24:11.491
So this kid who went AWOL in Daejeon,
this is the guy who killed No Ui-cheol?

24:11.575 --> 24:12.492
Yes.

24:12.576 --> 24:16.163
We realize you're busy, but could you
please help us out just this once?

24:16.663 --> 24:18.665
Yeah, we are very busy.

24:20.417 --> 24:23.545
And regarding
Professor No Ui-cheol's murder,

24:24.171 --> 24:26.173
we're doing everything we can right now.

24:26.256 --> 24:29.134
We identified a suspect
who he's on bad terms with.

24:29.217 --> 24:32.971
-Our boys are out on a stakeout now.
-I see.

24:33.054 --> 24:35.640
They're practically living at the station
and the scene,

24:35.724 --> 24:37.726
trying to find the murder weapon
and witnesses,

24:37.809 --> 24:41.104
really giving it their all,
and their wives want 'em back already.

24:41.605 --> 24:42.814
And…

24:42.898 --> 24:46.401
And now, you come in here saying
this missing person is a suspect.

24:46.485 --> 24:49.112
Without any leads.
Wouldn't that put us in a tough position--

24:49.196 --> 24:52.782
We have an official document issued
for your cooperation, so…

24:54.159 --> 24:56.286
We'd appreciate if you would work with us.

24:56.369 --> 24:58.079
-Yes, but we're busy--
-All right.

24:58.830 --> 25:02.250
We just have to let you know
if something comes up with those murders?

25:02.334 --> 25:03.835
Yeah. Uh, no.

25:03.919 --> 25:06.588
We'd really appreciate it if, uh…

25:08.089 --> 25:11.676
if you could share information
about any unnatural deaths too.

25:12.177 --> 25:13.512
-Everything?
-Yeah.

25:31.613 --> 25:33.532
All I've ever done is work.

25:33.615 --> 25:34.991
That's not a sin.

25:36.910 --> 25:39.079
My daughter just started middle school.

25:39.579 --> 25:41.790
What did I do wrong? Huh?

25:42.832 --> 25:43.917
Answer me, you bitch.

25:46.253 --> 25:48.129
For fuck's sake, man.

25:50.507 --> 25:53.176
These pricks are impossible.

26:05.981 --> 26:06.982
Whoops.

26:13.113 --> 26:14.739
How long do you think you can evade us?

27:46.081 --> 27:47.123
Yeah, hello?

27:47.874 --> 27:49.584
Gyeong-a, it's Sang-min.

27:50.293 --> 27:51.836
We hung out a few days ago.

27:53.880 --> 27:55.256
Can you talk for a second?

27:55.965 --> 27:58.218
How were you able to find my number?

27:59.594 --> 28:02.180
Well, I asked some of our friends
if they had it,

28:02.972 --> 28:06.476
and then I asked around to some
other people from elementary school.

28:10.563 --> 28:13.650
I thought I was clear.
I don't want to talk to you.

28:14.943 --> 28:17.320
But there's something I need to tell you.

28:18.113 --> 28:19.406
What is it?

28:22.617 --> 28:24.035
I got sextorted.

28:25.203 --> 28:26.079
I…

28:27.997 --> 28:30.041
I have no idea what to do right now.

28:31.042 --> 28:34.796
Just tell me the truth.
How did you find my number, really?

28:36.256 --> 28:41.010
Well, I was desperate… to get your number,

28:42.512 --> 28:44.389
so I asked my cop friend for it.

28:47.016 --> 28:48.435
I realize it was wrong.

28:52.063 --> 28:55.400
It was my only option.
I thought you could help.

28:56.860 --> 28:59.738
'Cause I thought
this could really be the end.

29:03.199 --> 29:04.492
It's not like

29:05.410 --> 29:06.411
I can just

29:07.495 --> 29:08.955
go to Seoul or anything.

29:09.956 --> 29:12.292
I can't even contact my parents right now.

29:12.375 --> 29:13.460
It's awful.

29:14.627 --> 29:16.129
I just…

29:19.424 --> 29:21.426
Right, that's a good call.

29:22.010 --> 29:25.388
It's expensive,
but hiring a private service is better.

29:26.014 --> 29:28.183
And cops are just not reliable.

29:29.559 --> 29:31.644
My girlfriend wanted to end things.

29:32.812 --> 29:33.813
So we did.

29:36.024 --> 29:38.067
I don't know what to tell my parents.

29:40.570 --> 29:41.780
That's it.

29:42.655 --> 29:46.201
Just be thankful that it hasn't
gotten out any more than it has.

29:48.411 --> 29:50.789
So, how did you get through it?

29:51.289 --> 29:52.207
Huh?

29:54.542 --> 29:56.252
How did you get over it?

30:01.257 --> 30:02.926
Get over it? Yeah.

30:03.843 --> 30:05.303
You saw me the other day.

30:07.388 --> 30:10.642
I'm suspicious of every man
who looks in my direction.

30:11.309 --> 30:13.353
"Has he already seen my video?"

30:15.480 --> 30:16.898
So, yeah.

30:17.816 --> 30:21.653
I still haven't really gotten over it,
exactly.

30:31.830 --> 30:32.831
Gyeong-a.

30:34.332 --> 30:35.291
Hmm?

30:37.210 --> 30:40.421
You can't blame yourself for it.
You just can't.

30:44.759 --> 30:46.261
You're doing really great.

31:12.120 --> 31:15.373
Hey, since you drove here,
you can go when you're sober.

31:15.456 --> 31:18.042
-Here, if you wanna shower.
-Right, thanks.

31:50.950 --> 31:52.577
You wanna sleep here?

32:01.628 --> 32:04.797
Babe, did something good happen?
Why do you look like that?

32:04.881 --> 32:07.258
It's nothing. I'm just happy.

32:07.967 --> 32:09.344
What?

32:11.471 --> 32:12.555
What's with you?

32:14.849 --> 32:16.768
-It's good.
-Going back in two days?

32:16.851 --> 32:19.062
-I think I'm going tomorrow.
-Again?

32:19.145 --> 32:22.690
Mm-hmm. The boss asked me
to work and help him out.

32:23.274 --> 32:24.609
So I said I would.

32:25.693 --> 32:29.405
It sucks, but we're getting married soon,
so I should be diligent.

32:30.823 --> 32:33.201
-I'm sorry.
-It's fine.

32:36.120 --> 32:38.331
I'll take you someplace nice
next time.

32:43.336 --> 32:44.754
Hey. Open up your trunk.

32:45.463 --> 32:47.256
-Why?
-Just open it.

32:47.340 --> 32:48.758
Why?

32:58.601 --> 32:59.477
Oppa!

33:00.186 --> 33:02.188
-What?
-Why'd you lie to me?

33:02.271 --> 33:03.940
You've got a terrible poker face.

33:04.816 --> 33:07.443
-I wasn't lying.
-You could've said you were going fishing.

33:07.527 --> 33:10.154
I wouldn't have gotten angry.
I'm really not that petty.

33:11.197 --> 33:12.323
Just go.

33:12.907 --> 33:15.326
Go have fun with your friends, okay?

33:17.036 --> 33:21.582
-I just didn't wanna hurt your feelings.
-Oppa! Let's always be honest, okay?

33:22.083 --> 33:24.752
I want us to tell the truth
to avoid issues down the line.

33:24.836 --> 33:26.546
-All right?
-Yes. You're right.

33:27.130 --> 33:29.674
We're getting married,
so I'll let this one go.

33:30.717 --> 33:32.760
You won't find a girl like me.
Treat me right!

33:32.844 --> 33:34.137
Okay, I'll do better.

33:34.220 --> 33:35.263
Let's go!

33:39.517 --> 33:42.729
I'm here
to get groceries with the guys. Yeah.

33:44.272 --> 33:45.940
Yeah, I miss you too, babe.

33:46.983 --> 33:50.528
I found a coffee shop here
that you'd love. It even has a terrace.

33:51.320 --> 33:52.405
Yes.

33:53.031 --> 33:55.533
I love you too. Bye.

33:56.284 --> 33:57.910
I'll call you back, okay?

33:57.994 --> 33:59.871
Bye.

34:00.580 --> 34:01.497
Gyeong-a.

34:02.331 --> 34:03.207
Gyeong-a.

34:05.168 --> 34:07.336
What? I thought
you said you were in Seoul.

34:07.420 --> 34:09.047
I wanted to surprise you.

34:46.209 --> 34:47.168
Oh…

35:28.876 --> 35:31.754
The warmth
of another person's embrace.

35:31.838 --> 35:34.298
I don't know
how I've gone so long without it.

35:34.799 --> 35:35.800
Mm-hmm.

35:36.717 --> 35:41.472
It's really amazing
how childhood friends can fall in love.

35:48.271 --> 35:49.355
Should I

35:50.523 --> 35:53.359
come back with you when you go to Seoul?

35:57.864 --> 35:58.781
Seoul?

35:59.866 --> 36:00.700
Mm-hmm.

36:01.284 --> 36:05.079
Well, you live in Seoul, so I…

36:05.746 --> 36:06.873
Hang on.

36:23.514 --> 36:25.224
I'm tired.

36:32.023 --> 36:33.858
NOT BAD
BUT WHY IS THE VIDEO SO SHORT?

36:38.196 --> 36:39.822
WE'RE GETTING MARRIED

36:39.906 --> 36:41.532
THANK YOU FOR COMING TO CELEBRATE

36:41.616 --> 36:43.868
What are you doing?

36:44.577 --> 36:46.120
Give me back my phone.

36:46.204 --> 36:47.788
What are you doing?

36:49.290 --> 36:50.499
What the hell?

36:53.502 --> 36:54.879
Didn't you say that you…

36:56.547 --> 36:58.132
…broke up with your girlfriend?

37:01.260 --> 37:03.346
I was gonna tell you.

37:03.429 --> 37:04.805
-I didn't get a chance.
-When?

37:04.889 --> 37:07.058
I was gonna tell you.

37:07.141 --> 37:10.603
I thought you were going out with me
because you already ended things.

37:12.897 --> 37:13.773
Listen, In-seon.

37:13.856 --> 37:17.193
-It's Gyeong-a now!
-Okay, fine, I know! Gyeong-a, come on!

37:17.276 --> 37:19.320
I'm telling you now!

37:19.403 --> 37:22.073
Telling me what, exactly?

37:22.156 --> 37:25.618
Just tell me
everything you lied about right now.

37:26.285 --> 37:28.579
What's really going on here?

37:58.567 --> 38:00.528
Oh, now we're in business.

38:03.906 --> 38:06.325
DELIVERY
MS. CHOI GYEONG-A

38:10.204 --> 38:12.498
This camera's great. Honey!

38:13.582 --> 38:15.543
-Look over here.
-What are you doing?

38:16.043 --> 38:18.004
You know. Come on, it's fun.

38:18.087 --> 38:20.840
What? Is this a video? Stop it.

38:20.923 --> 38:23.009
-What?
-Oh, my In-seon.

38:23.968 --> 38:26.012
-We're making memories.
-Just for us?

38:26.095 --> 38:27.513
So she wanted to?

38:38.899 --> 38:40.776
Did you really get sextorted?

38:40.860 --> 38:42.737
Why would
you look at my phone? Fuck.

38:42.820 --> 38:45.114
Tell me if that was real or not,
right now.

38:45.197 --> 38:46.407
All right, yeah.

38:46.490 --> 38:48.117
I made it up to sleep with you.

38:53.414 --> 38:55.499
You don't see me as a human. Is that it?

38:56.000 --> 38:57.960
-I'm just a piece of meat?
-Ugh, fucking bitch.

38:58.044 --> 39:00.338
-That you fuck and just walk away? Huh?
-Hey!

39:00.421 --> 39:02.673
-Listen, God damn it! Now!
-What? What? What?

39:02.757 --> 39:04.925
-You knew I had a girlfriend!
-What?

39:05.009 --> 39:08.095
Hey! You invited me into your bed!
So stop whining, you bitch.

39:08.596 --> 39:10.389
You said you broke up with her!

39:10.473 --> 39:12.600
-Shut the fuck up.
-Fine. All right, fine.

39:12.683 --> 39:14.935
Let's say I knew.
Does your girlfriend know?

39:15.019 --> 39:18.272
-Does she know you're having sex with me?
-Are you seriously threatening me?

39:18.356 --> 39:20.441
-Do your colleagues know?
-So you're threatening me?

39:20.524 --> 39:22.026
Yes, I am. Where's your phone?

39:22.109 --> 39:25.404
-Your girlfriend and friends should know!
-Stop that.

39:25.488 --> 39:27.948
You stupid little bitch.

39:28.032 --> 39:30.576
You fucking asshole!

39:30.659 --> 39:33.204
For fuck's sake!

39:33.287 --> 39:34.163
Hey!

39:34.246 --> 39:36.207
Hey, stop it.

39:36.707 --> 39:38.250
You fucking little bitch.

39:39.627 --> 39:40.544
Shut the fuck up.

39:41.128 --> 39:42.463
You fucking bitch!

39:44.465 --> 39:45.800
Shit! Can't you…

39:57.353 --> 40:00.272
CHOI IN-SEON, CHOI GYEONG-A

41:00.458 --> 41:02.710
Oh no. Oh no. Oh no. Oh no.

41:02.793 --> 41:04.879
What do I do? What do I do? What the fuck?

41:04.962 --> 41:07.756
The exact cause of the fire
and the number of casualties

41:07.840 --> 41:09.758
is still currently being investigated.

41:09.842 --> 41:13.512
The fire department sent 12 firefighters
and used several pieces of equipment

41:13.596 --> 41:15.181
as soon as they received the report

41:15.264 --> 41:17.516
and were able to extinguish the fire
within one hour.

41:17.600 --> 41:21.187
They have said that the cause of the fire
is still under investigation.

41:21.270 --> 41:24.064
Busanjin Police Station
identified the victim

41:24.148 --> 41:27.276
as a 29-year-old female
residing in Gyeongnam.

41:28.110 --> 41:31.071
Based on witness statements
and the security camera footage--

41:32.448 --> 41:35.701
-Around 5:00 a.m. today…
-Isn't that our neighborhood?

41:35.784 --> 41:40.372
-Hang on. Where did you say that was?
-It's across from Gujeon Church.

41:40.456 --> 41:41.749
-Gujeon Church.
-Gujeon?

41:41.832 --> 41:46.045
-Yeah. I heard the lady lived alone.
-Oh wow. This is awful.

41:46.128 --> 41:47.922
Know what else I heard? She was murdered.

41:48.005 --> 41:49.340
-Come on!
-Really?

41:49.423 --> 41:51.425
-Uh-huh.
-Stop spreading ridiculous rumors.

41:51.509 --> 41:53.969
Neighbors heard her
fighting with someone all night.

41:54.053 --> 41:55.387
-No way.
-Who said that?

41:55.471 --> 41:57.306
Do-jun's mother.

41:57.806 --> 42:01.060
You know that woman's always full of crap
and making stuff up.

42:01.560 --> 42:04.772
-Well, I don't totally believe her.
-See? Even you're not sure.

42:04.855 --> 42:07.608
-My God.
-I know. So tragic.

42:07.691 --> 42:09.401
Let it go.

42:14.031 --> 42:15.115
Well, then.

42:15.199 --> 42:16.992
…possibility of the fire being arson…

42:17.076 --> 42:19.328
How much do you believe her?

42:19.411 --> 42:21.121
-The city of Busan is…
-Huh?

42:24.750 --> 42:25.626
VICTIM CHOI GYEONG-A

42:25.709 --> 42:28.420
Well, it seems like
the girl was just drunk

42:28.504 --> 42:31.882
and just forgot to turn off the stove
before she went to bed.

42:31.966 --> 42:34.552
Also, we, uh,
looked through her call history,

42:34.635 --> 42:36.595
and she only kept in touch
with her parents.

42:36.679 --> 42:40.849
The other people on the list were,
uh, just… What was it? Her coworkers…

42:40.933 --> 42:43.018
-Oh, yeah, and the delivery man.
-Who is this?

42:43.102 --> 42:44.937
-I think…
-It's her friend.

42:45.020 --> 42:46.981
He didn't call on the day of the incident.

42:48.023 --> 42:50.609
So chances of her being a murder victim
are low,

42:50.693 --> 42:53.112
but we're doing an autopsy, so we'll see.

42:53.195 --> 42:54.697
Can we start the investigation?

42:54.780 --> 42:57.324
-What investigation? We have no warrant.
-There are procedures.

42:57.408 --> 43:00.494
I'm saying we should be open
to the idea that this was actually murder.

43:00.578 --> 43:02.496
Okay? I wanted you to share everything.

43:03.080 --> 43:05.165
You think all dead bodies
are murders cases?

43:05.249 --> 43:06.584
-God!
-Fuck! Shit.

43:14.466 --> 43:16.302
Hey, Gyeong-su. There you are.

43:16.927 --> 43:18.637
-Hey, give me the phone.
-Here.

43:21.515 --> 43:23.517
You know, uh, that girl, right?

43:24.476 --> 43:26.061
Yeah, you know her. Gyeong-a.

43:26.729 --> 43:27.980
Why? What's going on?

43:28.063 --> 43:28.939
BODY FOUND

43:29.023 --> 43:29.940
This is her.

43:31.650 --> 43:33.777
Apparently, she, uh… died.

43:33.861 --> 43:35.404
-Hey. Come here.
-Huh?

43:35.487 --> 43:37.406
Yeah. Okay. Get to work.

43:37.906 --> 43:39.742
All right. Come on, guys.

43:39.825 --> 43:41.452
Enough with this, already, huh?

43:41.535 --> 43:43.704
Now, we should just…

43:45.914 --> 43:48.208
-Yes, great job.
-No, look…

43:53.547 --> 43:55.007
Maybe next week.

44:28.499 --> 44:30.459
-Wait here.
-Yes, sir.

44:32.544 --> 44:34.004
Where is he?

44:34.088 --> 44:37.383
-Wait, why's he looking for him?
-He's police.

45:01.824 --> 45:03.450
Hey, where you going?

45:13.919 --> 45:14.920
Oh! Ah!

45:17.840 --> 45:18.966
Lee Tang.

45:23.804 --> 45:26.515
I can't believe how sloppy you are.

45:32.229 --> 45:34.857
You know the case in Gujeon-dong?

45:36.734 --> 45:38.026
It was you, huh?

46:06.472 --> 46:08.098
Oh, stand up, huh?

46:09.892 --> 46:11.393
We gotta go somewhere now.

46:14.396 --> 46:16.565
There's a lot we gotta talk about, kid.

46:17.483 --> 46:18.817
Just the two of us.

46:57.981 --> 47:00.067
-I manage the security cameras.
-Yong-jae.

47:00.150 --> 47:01.443
-What's wrong?
-Hey.

47:01.527 --> 47:04.655
-Someone stole the security footage drive.
-The cameras?

47:04.738 --> 47:06.615
-Yeah.
-You got a manual for this?

47:06.698 --> 47:08.659
-Let me see the photo.
-Who's in charge?

47:09.201 --> 47:10.369
I manage it all.

47:10.452 --> 47:13.163
-They're just for monitoring employees.
-Have you seen this person?

47:14.164 --> 47:15.374
Is this Gyeong-su?

47:16.083 --> 47:19.253
-I think he works here.
-He works here? Do you have his address?

47:19.878 --> 47:21.880
-Yeah, I have it.
-Let's go here first.

47:21.964 --> 47:24.675
Hey, hold on.
This isn't your turf.

47:24.758 --> 47:26.760
He's a murder suspect.
We should visit him.

47:26.844 --> 47:28.470
Are you kidding me right now?

47:28.971 --> 47:29.972
Listen, man.

47:30.681 --> 47:33.433
I did some digging, and apparently,
you got suspended in Daejeon.

47:34.184 --> 47:36.812
I looked the other way since you're
one of us, but stay in your lane.

47:36.895 --> 47:39.022
I was looking into a guy in a murder case.

47:39.106 --> 47:41.358
-I was suspended--
-How can we trust a suspended detective?

47:41.441 --> 47:43.151
What's not to trust?
I have no reason to lie.

47:43.235 --> 47:44.903
Besides, we got nothin' to lose anymore.

47:44.987 --> 47:48.574
-There are procedures and orders we need--
-Stop it. Come on.

47:49.575 --> 47:50.534
This man.

47:51.827 --> 47:53.662
You're sure that he's your employee?

47:53.745 --> 47:55.455
Yeah, in the fish section.

47:56.999 --> 47:58.584
Okay. I say we all go.

47:59.543 --> 48:00.752
Follow me.

48:01.503 --> 48:02.921
What?

48:21.315 --> 48:22.691
Look at this punk.

48:35.037 --> 48:37.581
-Kwak, go and see Ha Sang-min.
-Yes, sir.

48:37.664 --> 48:40.000
-The delivery man, as well.
-Okay, you got it.

48:40.083 --> 48:43.420
-You get all footage near the house.
-Hey. Come here.

48:45.047 --> 48:47.049
Follow Detective Kwak's interviews.

48:47.925 --> 48:49.134
-Not Lee Tang?
-I'll do that.

48:49.217 --> 48:51.970
Stay close with them
and report back on what they're all up to.

48:52.054 --> 48:54.014
-…all needs to be done now.
-Hurry.

48:54.097 --> 48:55.849
-Come on.
-Uh, okay. I'll call you.

49:00.103 --> 49:02.105
It's called Neisseria gonorrhoeae.

49:02.189 --> 49:04.358
You have heard of gonorrhea, haven't you?

49:05.943 --> 49:09.279
It's a bacteria,
transmitted through sexual intercourse.

49:10.030 --> 49:14.576
But there's no need to worry.
It can be fully cured with antibiotics.

49:15.452 --> 49:19.373
Oh, and no sexual intercourse
for the time being.

49:23.001 --> 49:24.628
I was in bed sick.

49:27.756 --> 49:30.175
Honey, I got some not great news.

49:30.258 --> 49:31.635
Babe, wait.

49:31.718 --> 49:34.137
No, let me… let me talk first.

49:34.221 --> 49:35.347
Hmm? What is it?

49:36.598 --> 49:38.475
I have gonorrhea.

49:39.351 --> 49:40.352
Just how…

49:41.269 --> 49:43.605
I wanted to bring it up to you first, but…

49:45.482 --> 49:48.402
-Hmm.
-I'm so sorry, baby.

49:49.611 --> 49:51.947
It was a mistake. It only happened once.

49:52.531 --> 49:54.741
-What are you saying?
-I wasn't even gonna go.

49:54.825 --> 49:56.660
But my friends were insisting

49:56.743 --> 49:59.121
I'm not gonna have fun anymore
once I'm married.

49:59.871 --> 50:02.040
They literally just dragged me along.

50:02.124 --> 50:04.042
Oppa, I'm so sorry.

50:06.003 --> 50:08.171
It was really just a stupid mistake.

50:09.214 --> 50:11.133
Wow.

50:11.216 --> 50:13.552
-You're a fucking bitch.
-What?

50:14.511 --> 50:15.887
-Huh.
-Oh…

50:16.596 --> 50:18.140
I'm so sorry.

50:18.890 --> 50:20.976
Hey, Hyeon-ji.

50:24.229 --> 50:25.522
-Just fuck off.
-Oppa--

50:25.605 --> 50:26.773
Shit, man.

50:38.243 --> 50:40.746
Mr. Ha Sang-min?

50:41.413 --> 50:43.415
-Yes?
-Ah.

50:47.961 --> 50:49.838
You know Choi Gyeong-a. Isn't that right?

50:51.548 --> 50:54.176
-Yeah.
-And you went to Gujeon-dong.

50:54.259 --> 50:55.177
Yeah.

50:56.136 --> 50:58.805
-And you slept with her.
-Yes.

50:59.556 --> 51:01.767
-But you didn't kill her?
-Right.

51:03.101 --> 51:04.061
Hmm.

51:04.644 --> 51:07.564
So you found out
from the news she was dead?

51:07.647 --> 51:08.690
Yes.

51:10.275 --> 51:12.277
That so?

51:15.322 --> 51:16.740
Why was she killed?

51:19.743 --> 51:23.663
Because, from what I heard, there were
sounds of fighting at her apartment.

51:25.707 --> 51:26.792
Uh…

51:29.461 --> 51:30.295
At what time?

51:30.378 --> 51:33.799
I don't know, um… anything about that.

51:38.095 --> 51:39.304
From now on,

51:40.597 --> 51:42.140
let's not lie anymore.

51:43.266 --> 51:45.602
Unless you wanna
complicate the matter at hand.

51:47.687 --> 51:50.899
Oh. I… I remember now. I, uh…

51:52.609 --> 51:57.155
Actually, I'd started dated Gyeong-a
while I had a girlfriend still.

51:57.239 --> 52:00.033
And Gyeong-a had known that
going into the relationship.

52:01.118 --> 52:05.956
But… she eventually happened to learn
that I, uh…

52:06.039 --> 52:09.501
-Uh… was actually engaged… to her.
-Okay.

52:10.085 --> 52:12.129
-Ah.
-So, that…

52:13.797 --> 52:17.217
I guess it made her feel lied to,
and she raised her voice.

52:17.300 --> 52:19.136
-Aah.
-That brought on an argument.

52:19.219 --> 52:20.220
And?

52:20.971 --> 52:22.639
You beat her head in? Like that?

52:24.391 --> 52:25.600
What are you… No.

52:31.523 --> 52:32.941
I really didn't kill her.

52:34.442 --> 52:37.237
Oh, you son of a bitch.
You fucking asshole.

52:37.320 --> 52:39.656
I was thinking about setting you free.

52:44.870 --> 52:46.746
Shameless. It's true, huh?

52:47.455 --> 52:50.917
Almost had me fooled.
You're so, so brazen.

52:51.001 --> 52:52.586
Do you have a warrant for that?

52:52.669 --> 52:55.088
-A what?
-I said, do you have a warrant for that?

52:55.922 --> 52:56.756
Right.

52:57.674 --> 52:58.550
-Uh…
-What?

52:58.633 --> 53:01.678
I'd like my attorney present
for when you take my statement.

53:02.470 --> 53:05.265
It's always you half-assed idiots, huh?

53:05.348 --> 53:07.058
-Huh?
-I want my lawyer.

53:07.142 --> 53:09.311
Run your mouths, hmm?

53:09.394 --> 53:11.104
It's fine. You won't get caught.

53:12.647 --> 53:14.566
I didn't even kill her. Fuck.

53:17.444 --> 53:19.779
But… I kinda ran away.

53:20.614 --> 53:23.450
If what you're saying is true,
I should stay in Busan.

53:25.535 --> 53:26.578
Now it's different.

53:26.661 --> 53:29.039
That hunch you felt
could be part of your powers.

53:29.539 --> 53:32.542
But if you feel that way again,
you gotta be cautious.

53:33.793 --> 53:37.130
You should probably lay low.
Don't contact me. Turn your phone off.

53:38.173 --> 53:39.674
I'll see what I can do, okay?

53:48.266 --> 53:49.643
Let's see…

53:54.397 --> 53:55.690
Ugh, come on.

53:55.774 --> 53:59.527
Why isn't there any paper
in this dumb, shitty house?

53:59.611 --> 54:02.280
You're not…
you're not a cop, are you?

54:05.659 --> 54:06.618
I am.

54:07.410 --> 54:08.578
Well, used to be.

54:09.079 --> 54:10.789
Why… why are you doing this?

54:15.502 --> 54:17.462
All right, let me ask you a question.

54:19.297 --> 54:20.423
There's this

54:21.007 --> 54:22.801
bastard I'm trying to locate.

54:23.843 --> 54:25.053
That dumbass

54:25.971 --> 54:29.057
somehow zeroes in on shitheads like you

54:29.599 --> 54:31.351
and kills them, huh?

54:32.143 --> 54:33.395
Then, shouldn't he be

54:34.604 --> 54:38.316
already well on his way,
you little shit stain?

54:42.028 --> 54:43.238
This is boring.

54:45.573 --> 54:46.950
So boring.

55:09.973 --> 55:14.060
Will you not kill me
if I tell you the truth?

55:15.687 --> 55:17.272
What?

55:24.112 --> 55:25.739
Will I keep you alive, you said?

55:26.364 --> 55:27.240
Yes.

55:30.702 --> 55:32.662
So you admit you killed her, then?

55:36.207 --> 55:37.125
Yeah.

55:37.959 --> 55:39.878
All right, go ahead.

55:41.504 --> 55:42.797
Write it.

55:48.595 --> 55:49.554
Uh…

55:50.930 --> 55:53.308
Choi In-seon…

55:56.311 --> 55:59.731
I, HA SANG-MIN, MURDERED CHOI IN-SEON,
AND I SHOW MY REMORSE THROUGH DEATH

55:59.814 --> 56:00.732
Huh.

56:04.486 --> 56:06.780
He didn't say how he killed Gyeong-a.

56:07.989 --> 56:09.074
God.

56:10.700 --> 56:12.327
Can't do much writing now.

56:13.661 --> 56:14.579
Shit.

56:18.083 --> 56:20.502
God, he just has no common sense.

56:21.169 --> 56:25.799
Apology letters should always state
the when, why, and how.

56:26.299 --> 56:28.426
Damn millennials.

56:38.269 --> 56:40.855
This is the apartment
management office.

56:40.939 --> 56:44.943
There was a fire recently due to
an induction cooktop in one of the units.

56:45.026 --> 56:46.945
When leaving the house, please be sure

56:47.028 --> 56:50.115
to turn off the cooktop
or unplug it entirely.

56:50.198 --> 56:53.076
Additionally, do not leave
paper towels near the cooktop,

56:53.159 --> 56:54.369
as it may cause a fire.

57:09.759 --> 57:11.636
That Lee Tang, or Lee Gyeong-su,

57:12.303 --> 57:14.055
he's probably already left Busan.

57:14.639 --> 57:16.599
He had to have left some clues behind.

57:16.683 --> 57:17.892
Something helpful.

57:18.726 --> 57:22.021
That's true. He didn't have time
to stop at his house.

57:22.105 --> 57:23.815
There's gotta be something there.

58:06.691 --> 58:07.859
Anyone there?

58:09.777 --> 58:11.696
Hello?

58:15.325 --> 58:16.493
Anyone home?

58:19.454 --> 58:21.164
Is this the management office?

58:22.207 --> 58:25.960
It's the police.
Where's the master key for this place?

58:28.004 --> 58:28.922
Huh?

58:30.256 --> 58:31.925
It was stolen? By who?

58:32.717 --> 58:33.968
What do you mean?

58:36.012 --> 58:37.430
Don't you hear that sound?

58:38.389 --> 58:40.183
No, what sound? I don't hear it.

58:53.321 --> 58:55.698
FUEL
DO NOT HEAT

59:00.912 --> 59:03.414
What the…
What's with all this smoke?

59:06.042 --> 59:07.752
Is that from a fire extinguisher?

59:10.672 --> 59:12.006
Has he been by already?
